From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 10:38:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: s800x: Give the A9 iPhones' battery
 temperature limits

The SN2400 charger now follows the battery temperature against the
monitored battery's limits. The ADT has none; use the usual Li-ion
ones: charge from 0 to 45 C, at full input from 10 to 40 C.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800x-iphone.dtsi | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800x-iphone.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800x-iphone.dtsi
index a6baf77a7..4bb2c49d0 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800x-iphone.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/s800x-iphone.dtsi
@@ -98,6 +98,13 @@ &disp0 {
 / {
 	battery_info: battery {
 		compatible = "simple-battery";
+		/*
+		 * The charger's input follows the battery temperature: off
+		 * outside 0..45 C, reduced outside 10..40 C. The ADT gives no
+		 * limits; these are the usual ones for Li-ion cells.
+		 */
+		operating-range-celsius = <0 45>;
+		alert-celsius = <10 40>;
 	};
 };
 
